meta {
  name: List Managed Meta Pages
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/meta/pages?tenant_id={{tenantId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

docs {
  Every Meta Page the selected tenant's stored token manages, as
  { page_id, name } — so the mapping screen can offer pages by name instead of
  asking an admin to paste raw numeric Meta Page ids.

  Wraps the Graph API GET /me/accounts, cursor-paged. A TypeScript port of
  meta-sync-scripts/common/graph_api.py::get_managed_pages, which was the only
  implementation until now.

  Requires super_admin and an explicit ?tenant_id=: the call spends that
  tenant's stored Meta credentials.

  Regression checks:
    * response contains no access_token at ANY nesting level. The Graph request
      asks for fields=id,name and never requests the token, so there is no
      secret in scope to leak — not merely one that is stripped on the way out.
    * tenant with no integration, or an inactive one -> 404
    * caller below super_admin                       -> 403
}
